Count the command's own arguments towards the Windows length limit.
When xargs checked that the quoted items fit on the Windows command
line it counted only the items, not the command and the arguments
given with it, so a command with long arguments could still be given a
command line longer than Windows allows. Windows then refused to run
it, and xargs exited with status 126, or, under Wine, the line was cut
short and items were silently lost.

Start the count with the quoted length of the fixed arguments.

